            'US airlines move about 61,000 tons of cargo a day, according to Airlines for America, much of it in passenger-aircraft bellies. With 18,520 flights canceled in four days, that capacity vanished just when it was needed most. Delta Cargo suspended special services such as express, pharma and live animals until midnight Saturday; American Airlines Cargo was back to normal on Sunday; and Expeditors and Woodland Group warned of backlogs, missed connections and reduced capacity at several gateways over the weekend.',
